From 1ad2ec4e6a864a0a9599c79ff31a61bde5c64827 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 17:04:26 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] test(v2): functional coverage of the legacy bridge and
 chained legacy transactions

feature_v2_legacy_bridge.py migrates legacy coins to V2 on two nodes:
- legacy coinbases fund P2PKH, 2-of-3 P2SH and P2PK coins and a 25-deep
  MiniWallet chain of legacy transactions, relayed and mined;
- version 7 transactions spend them through the P2PKH bridge (modes 0 and
  1), the P2SH bridge (2-of-3 ECDSA) and P2SH(OP_TRUE) MiniWallet coins,
  creating V2 outputs, which are then spent natively;
- a legacy transaction spending a V2 coin gives
  bad-txns-legacy-spends-v2-coin;
- a P2PK coin gives bad-txns-v2-legacy-coin-template through the bridge
  and is spent by a version 2 transaction;
- invalidating the bridge block restores the legacy coin in the chain
  state, and reconsidering it spends it again;
- a restart keeps the UTXO set hash and the coins, which stay bridgeable;
- a node started with -coinbaseversion=7 mines V2 coinbases that
  MiniWalletV7 finds and spends.

MiniWalletV7 gains generate(): it mines to raw(4e) and records the
coinbase outputs it owns (the branched V0-leaf output over OP_TRUE, or a
plain-script output with no branches), since scantxoutset matches legacy
scripts only; get_utxo() skips immature coinbases.

Chronik assertions (is_legacy after a reorg) wait for T1-11.

Rebase onto coordinator 276 (81e8ef1774): funds legacy coins from
v7tx.LegacyMiniWallet instead of the framework's (V2) MiniWallet.

Tier: V2

Coordinator integration provenance (reference405):
0004-legacy-default-explicit-native-wallet.patch: Legacy default and explicit native wallet are bridge functional-coverage behavior, not early pure-native wallet semantics.
All60 authored input payloads retained, with prerequisite-aware same-purpose splits; distinct legacy-index and inherited CXX compatibility remain independent. Pre-format source equals exact403+all60 control tree95718fceff83364b74294a751bd752b2f1a4e384. Only pinnedRuff import/format cleanup follows. Original author commands/hashes are historical reference evidence, not combined405 approval. Reference OFF/native/Rust full gates are preserved separately; combined compile/runtime NOT_RUN.

Coordinator prefix adapter: preserve canonical endpoint behavior at this API/feature consumer; exact source-only per-tree transformations and first-owner ledger retained in final507 delivery. No historical-prefix runtime claim.
